  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a qualitative Q-methodology study in a single Chinese city, which may limit direct generalizability to other national or institutional contexts.",
      "what": "Using Q methodology, this study maps how young residents in Qingdao, China, perceive the state's youth-friendly city policies. It identifies three distinct youth viewpoints that prioritize institutional fairness, everyday affordability, and secure opportunities over the state's growth- and spectacle-driven urban development.",
      "why": "It demonstrates a misalignment between state-led, human-capital-focused urban planning and the actual lived aspirations of young citizens, conceptualizing this gap as a form of spatial injustice termed discursive deprivation."
    }
